    "result_text": "The implementation is complete. The `ownerSegment` feature is fully implemented and its tests (Cp55) pass, along with all other previously-passing tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the Owner API, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../util/OwnerSegments.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper following the existing util convention (`AgeBands`, `Localities`, etc.):\n   - `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - `AREA` = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n   - Returns `tier + \"_\" + area`.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it), documented with the full spec.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the MapStruct mapping. It uses the **effective** membership level (the stored `membershipLevel` when present, otherwise the derived one \u2014 mirroring the existing `membershipLevel` mapping) and the locality from `Localities.region(postcode, city)`.\n\n**Test results:**\n- `Cp55Tests` (this task's spec): **both tests pass** \u2014 `STANDARD_METRO` for a known region and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one.\n- Full suite: 68 tests, only 2 failures remain \u2014 `Cp23Tests` and `Cp39Tests`.\n\n**Important note on those 2 failures:** they are **pre-existing and unrelated** to this task. They concern `membershipLevel` capping on owner *creation* (a separate \"tier-gold\"/capping challenge). I verified this by removing all of my changes and running those two tests in isolation \u2014 they fail identically at baseline. My changes are purely additive (a new util, a new mapping, a new read-only OpenAPI field) and cannot affect `membershipLevel`. Fixing them would require implementing an unrelated feature outside this task's specification.",
